      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For contrast, consider a brute enforcer who relies purely on instinct and muscle, representing raw chaos against your detective's order. You could also introduce a slick, charming con artist with sharp observational skills but fundamentally rotten morality. Finally, a street-smart informant who operates in the moral grey areas, valuing information above all else, would create fascinating friction with your principled lead. These characters will force your protagonist out of purely intellectual problems and into visceral danger.",
